40,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some interesting things! It looks like we have plenty of help for software, but finding people for field work or supervisors is a real struggle. Our logistics advisers are also just sitting there!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings suggest a clear pattern. Our most successful exits were in back-office financial tooling, while our failure involved physical premises and hourly staff. Furthermore, specialized service providers show much stronger customer retention than general retail tools.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,May,,"My findings are a bit worrying. Our reserves are being drained by equipment and stock costs way faster than we planned. Plus, our credit line only helps if we have physical stock to lean on.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that software companies just give us their own numbers, but things with hardware or depots let us check for ourselves! But the hardware stuff makes the audit take way longer and costs a lot of money!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings confirm a pattern of delays. Companies dealing with medical records or financial data face significantly longer security reviews. Additionally, hardware assembly is prone to supply chain shocks, whereas pure software has been much more reliable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, that's a huge point! If hardware is slow to deploy and hard to staff, we might be in trouble. But @May, you said the credit line likes physical stock, right? That's a tricky trade-off!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,George,,"It is indeed a trade-off, @Mio. However, we must prioritize stability. My data shows that companies with physical operations and hourly crews are our highest risk for total loss, whereas specialized tooling has proven resilient.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly, @George. But we're bleeding cash on equipment! If we go for software, we can't borrow against it. We need a balance—something that doesn't drain us but keeps the bank happy. This is getting complicated!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if software companies just tell us what they want us to believe, isn't that scary? I like that we can check the hardware numbers, even if the audit is a big, expensive headache! Which one is worse?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, the risk of unreliable reporting is significant, but the risk of a product never reaching the customer is worse. We must weigh the cost of audits against the cost of total deployment failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm worried about the people side! If we pick something with field crews or supervisors, we're looking at a four-month wait just to hire. We have logistics advisers, but they aren't doing anything yet!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,George,,"@Mio, that confirms my suspicion. The operational burden of managing physical crews is a liability we cannot afford, especially if the hiring process is that sluggish. We should lean toward specialized software.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, I hear you, but we can't ignore the bank! If we go pure software, we have zero security for our credit line. We need something that balances risk with actual financial leverage.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we pick software, we're just trusting their dashboards! I don't like that. Maybe something that has a little bit of hardware but isn't too messy? That way we can check the numbers!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, a hybrid approach might be risky. My data shows that hardware assembly is vulnerable to shortages and medical or financial data triggers long security delays. We need a solution that avoids both supply chain shocks and regulatory bottlenecks.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm starting to think we should avoid anything that needs a lot of field staff or supervisors. It sounds like a nightmare to hire for! Let's see the candidates and find something we can actually support.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,George,,I agree. We must avoid the operational pitfalls of hourly crews and physical premises. I will be looking for a candidate that offers the stability of specialized tooling and strong customer retention.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm still worried about the cash flow, but I'm listening. If we can find a candidate that doesn't bleed us dry on follow-on calls but still gives us some leverage, I'm in. Let's see the options!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm just hoping for something that doesn't make the audit a total nightmare but still lets me check the numbers! I can't stand the thought of just guessing! Let's see who the candidates are!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. We need a candidate that avoids the high-friction zones: no complex hardware assembly, no medical or financial data that triggers long security reviews, and no reliance on hard-to-hire field crews. Let's evaluate the candidates.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
