65,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Looking at these, Fabric Loop sounds like a hiring nightmare with those sorting facilities! Harvest Sensor has hardware, but maybe our logistics advisers can finally help? I'm leaning toward Harvest Sensor or Ledger Bridge!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,George,,"Fabric Loop is far too risky given our history with physical premises and hourly crews. Ledger Bridge fits the profile of our most successful exits—quiet, back-office financial tooling. I vote for Ledger Bridge.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,May,,"Wait, @George, Ledger Bridge is pure software! That means zero security for our credit line and more drain on our reserves. Harvest Sensor has physical stock we can actually borrow against. I vote Harvest Sensor.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I don't like Ledger Bridge because I can't check their numbers! But Harvest Sensor has hardware, which means the audit will be super expensive and slow. I'll vote for Harvest Sensor because I want real proof!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, Ledger Bridge handles payment records, which my data suggests triggers a three-quarter security review. Clinic Scheduler has the same issue with medical records. Fabric Loop is an operational risk. Harvest Sensor is the most viable. I vote Harvest Sensor.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, you've convinced me! If the software options are stuck in security reviews for months, we can't wait. Harvest Sensor seems like the best balance. I vote Harvest Sensor!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, I hadn't considered the security review delay for financial data. While I prefer the stability of the tooling, a nine-month wait is unacceptable. I change my vote to Harvest Sensor.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,May,,It looks like we've found a consensus! I'm happy to go with Harvest Sensor. It gives us the physical assets we need for the credit line and avoids the security bottlenecks. I vote Harvest Sensor.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Rin,,"I'm so happy we all agree! Even if the audit is a bit of a pain, I'd much rather have real numbers than just a dashboard. Harvest Sensor it is! I vote Harvest Sensor!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"It is the most logical choice. It avoids the regulatory delays of medical and financial data, the operational risks of sorting facilities, and provides the verifiable data and assets the others require. I vote Harvest Sensor.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm just so glad we worked this out together! Harvest Sensor sounds like a great adventure, and I can't wait to see those sensors in the field!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
